notes               = "Untitled in source. Six lines, and the whole poem is one physical fact used as feeling: he goes hot at the sight of her and his shadow sinks into the snow, which is what a warm thing does to snow. Winter is months 10-12 → +622 = 2008. Imported as a draft with machine / lantern layers; ===translation=== left for Ben."
draft               = true

===persian===

در کوچهٔ پر برف تو
به انتظار ایستاده‌ام
هوا آفتابی‌ست
تو را می‌بینم که خندان می‌آیی
من داغ می‌شوم
سایه‌ام در برف فرو می‌رود...
زمستان ۱۳۸۶

===machine===

In your snow-filled lane
I am standing, waiting.
The weather is sunny.
I see you coming, laughing.
I go hot —
and my shadow sinks away into the snow...
Winter 1386

===lantern===

In your snow-filled lane
I am standing, waiting.
The weather is sunny.
I see you coming, laughing.
I go hot,
and my shadow sinks away into the snow...

Winter 1386

===translation===

===footnotes===

A warm object standing on snow melts a hollow and settles into it. The poem lets that be the
whole of what happens when he sees her.
